{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1457238-is-jareth-an-owl-pooka","id":1457238,"title":"Is Jareth an Owl Pooka?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-19T16:26:21-07:00","id":1457238,"title":"Is Jareth an Owl Pooka?","content":"What it says on the tin. David Bowie's character in the Labyrinth is the Goblin King, which suggests a link to Nockers. Certainly is looks suggest Sidhe. But, although it is subtle, his hair and makeup suggest the owl he regularly turns into. More importantly, he never really answers a straight question truthfully. Normally he either evades or launches an accusation. He eludes to the truth, but never really says it. <br /> <br /> Jareth makes a lot of sense as an Unseelie Owl Pooka. What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T16:40:57-07:00","id":1457239,"title":"","content":"You definitely have a strong point on the validity of that way of approaching the character. I'm not sure I would ultimately choose it if I wanted the over all BBEG role he plays in the film, but I would be happy to see it as the starting point for a character to be played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T20:27:44-07:00","id":1457245,"title":"","content":"Other Fae have the power to shapechange than just Pooka. They just need the right Art, Realm, and sufficient points. I think the character would fit best into another Kith likely Sidhe. Pooka isn't the right match once you consider all the other traits. He's definitely Unseelie though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T07:58:59-07:00","id":1457269,"title":"","content":"Could be. But I would say he is an Unseelie Sidhe. His favored owl form could be the result of an Art, a Treasure or a Merit. Him being unable or unwilling to answer a straight question with a straight answer is pretty standard fae behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T20:25:19-07:00","id":1457314,"title":"","content":"Or maybe a Strega...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3670-spook359","name":"Spook359","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3670_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T20:29:10-07:00","id":1457315,"title":"","content":"One of the True Fey?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T18:45:44-07:00","id":1457360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1457238-is-jareth-an-owl-pooka?p=1457315#post1457315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the True Fey?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the film predates &quot;Changeling: The Dreaming&quot; or even any game like &quot;Night Fantastic&quot; or D&amp;D's fairy supplements that allowed one to play the Fay, you're right of course. I simply thought Unseelie Owl Pooka would be the strongest way to play Jareth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T18:48:43-07:00","id":1457361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spook359</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1457238-is-jareth-an-owl-pooka?p=1457314#post1457314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe a Strega...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Strega have many of Jateth's gifts. The strongest argument against Jareth as Owl Pooka is his time manipulation powers. The Sidhe seem to be the best at time manipulation. It's a major power of theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T18:52:36-07:00","id":1457362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1457238-is-jareth-an-owl-pooka?p=1457269#post1457269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be. But I would say he is an Unseelie Sidhe. His favored owl form could be the result of an Art, a Treasure or a Merit. Him being unable or unwilling to answer a straight question with a straight answer is pretty standard fae behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>His time manipulation powers favor your argument. And of course as &quot;Labyrinth&quot; predates C:tD by eight years the influence goes the other way. Still, Jateth's avoidance of the simple truth (unless he uses it to spin further lies) goes well beyond traditional fay ambiguity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T18:54:09-07:00","id":1457363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1457238-is-jareth-an-owl-pooka?p=1457239#post1457239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You definitely have a strong point on the validity of that way of approaching the character. I'm not sure I would ultimately choose it if I wanted the over all BBEG role he plays in the film, but I would be happy to see it as the starting point for a character to be played.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, it's all interpretation based on minor details. &quot;Labyrinth&quot; predates our beloved game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T14:38:24-07:00","id":1457427,"title":"","content":"I suspect that Jareth has always influenced by take on the true fey, along with Willy Wonka, Terpsichore from Xanadu, Evil from Time Bandits, Nicodemus from The Secret of NIMH, The Childlike Empress from The Never-Ending Story, The Horned King from The Black Cauldron, Jack O'the Green and the Lord of Darkness from Legend, the Nome King from Return to Oz, the King of the Moon and Vulcan and Venus from The Adventures of Baron Munchausen, the White Witch from The Lion The Witch &amp; The Wardrobe, and at least half the cast of The Phantom Tollbooth. (Obviously, I grew up in the 80s.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-22-2021, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T17:26:48-07:00","id":1457440,"title":"","content":"Born in 1960 and never dropped kids movies from my viewing. My mother often said of kids films that A) they still try to tell stories, and B) the lives an experiences of women and children ( a major part of her life) were often more realistically dealt with in children's film. In fact she noticed a serious lack of realistic depictions of the lives of women and children in most adult media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T16:29:04-07:00","id":1462940,"title":"","content":"Watching it a couple weeks ago, I came to the same conclusion.<br /> Jareth is an Owl Pooka with an Oneiromancy 2 Treasure orb and a bunch of Chimera to fill out a daydream. The entire movie is just him musing some Glamour off a Dreamer, Sarah.<br /> Everyone saying no is just trying too hard to make WoD characters fit into DnD cookiecutter molds. It doesn't help that the writers kept trying the same nonsense tying Kith/Clan to Personality for the players that couldn't figure out that part themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25819-wrxsv","name":"wrxsv","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}